Error [jet.StringViewOutlivesOwner]: An owned `String` cannot fill a `View<str>` slot
  --> tests/ui/ownership/owner_backed_collection_rejects_plain_string_as_view_str_field.jet:16:29
    |
 16 |     return TitleView{value: value}
    |                             ^^^^^
 Why: `View<str>` needs a zero-copy window from `.trim()` / `.after()` / `.before()` (or an already-tracked string-view binding); a plain `String` place owns its buffer instead
 Fix: Bind a window with `.trim()`/`.after()`/`.before()`, return a `View` of the owning element and read the field through it, or store an owned `String` field and copy with `.copy()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2307
